        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "We develop an equity asset-pricing framework grounded in Kyle’s (1985) model of strategic informed trading, in which the equilibrium price-impact coefficient  $ \\lambda $ governs how trading activity is impounded into prices. Using CRSP daily and monthly data for all equities in the CRSP universe from 2020 to 2025, we construct firm-month estimates of signed order flow and of  $ \\lambda $ itself, via both a direct within-month price-impact regression and an Amihud-style illiquidity ratio. We then test their ability to forecast the cross-section of subsequent stock returns.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                1076,
                1084,
                1221
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
